{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"fce04f9f3ba52a55","x":-240,"y":-840,"width":2440,"height":1520,"type":"text","text":""},
		{"id":"8dc554a51e599f52","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n\nA[Start] --> B[Get all table documents]\n\nB --> C{Any tables?}\n\nC -->|No| D[End]\n\nC -->|Yes| E[For each table]\n\nE --> F[Get columns]\n\nF --> G{Columns found?}\n\nG -->|No| E\n\nG -->|Yes| H[Query LLM]\n\nH --> I{Valid response?}\n\nI -->|No| E\n\nI -->|Yes| J[Update table metadata]\n\nJ --> K[Update column metadata]\n\nK --> E\n\nE --> L[Print final stats]\n\nL --> M[End]\n```\n","x":-200,"y":-800,"width":760,"height":1440},
		{"id":"015409ce10c0f6c3","x":680,"y":-800,"width":1020,"height":220,"type":"text","text":"### Problem Statement:\nThe task involves inferring metadata by generating `embedding_inputs`, `descriptions`, `tags`, and `embedding_vectors`. Currently, the LLM is called sequentially for each table, which increases processing time. The accuracy of the responses is only around 30–40%, and the process has high space complexity. Additionally, the focus so far has been primarily on generating `embedding_vectors` rather than improving overall metadata quality."},
		{"id":"509c6a914abfb1ef","x":580,"y":-317,"width":1580,"height":237,"type":"text","text":"```mermaid  \n%%{init: {'theme': 'default', 'themeVariables': { 'background': '#ffffff' }}}%%  \nflowchart LR  \n    F1[MongoDBMetadataProcessor] --> P2[Connect to MongoDB Collections<br>Initialize OpenAI LLM]  \n    P2 --> PB1[Sequential Table Processing - One-by-One<br>High Inference Time for n Tables]  \n    PB1 --> P4[Process Each Table:<br>Clean Label → Get Columns → Query LLM]  \n    P4 --> P5[Generate Embeddings & Update MongoDB<br>Return Results with Performance Issues]  \n```\n"},
		{"id":"e502933a4ea2ffbe","x":2480,"y":-840,"width":1120,"height":960,"type":"text","text":""},
		{"id":"3eca265221f03f1e","x":2520,"y":-780,"width":777,"height":200,"type":"text","text":"### Problem Statement:\nAfter improving descriptions and `embedding_inputs`, we moved to relationship inference. We added a `referencing_tables` field that recorded tables referenced via each table’s primary keys, but the inferred relationships were inaccurate."},
		{"id":"986bbf58aa5252d2","x":680,"y":-550,"width":1020,"height":190,"type":"text","text":"### Solution:\nWe implemented a batching process, grouping four tables at a time and making separate LLM calls for each table. This reduced program execution time by 50%. Additionally, we refined and stabilized the system prompts, which improved the quality of the generated descriptions and `embedding_inputs`."},
		{"id":"52cc7c59b4e4b9b6","x":2520,"y":-525,"width":777,"height":208,"type":"text","text":"### Solution:\nWe addressed this by separating `foreign_keys_referencing_tables` and `primary_keys_referencing_tables`. We also included the linking columns, table names, relationship types, and detailed relationship descriptions, which improved the accuracy of the inferred relationships."},
		{"id":"4cd6b6257c383c61","x":-240,"y":-1040,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"# First Iteration "},
		{"id":"d043fe0438c95f7f","x":2520,"y":-198,"width":980,"height":200,"type":"text","text":"```mermaid\n%%{init: {'theme': 'default', 'themeVariables': { 'background': '#ffffff' }}}%%\n\nflowchart LR\n\n  \n\nS1[Separate Fields:\n\nforeign_keys_referencing_tables\n\nprimary_keys_referencing_tables] --> S2[Added Details:\n\nLinking Columns\n\nTable Names\n\nRelationship Types\n\nDetailed Descriptions] --> S3[Relationship Inference]\n\n  \n\nstyle S3 fill:#c8e6c9\n```\n"},
		{"id":"d661b1665b695b7a","x":2480,"y":-1040,"width":386,"height":80,"type":"text","text":"# Second Iteration\n"}
	],
